== Review from Previous Class
<review-from-previous-class>
The class opened with a brief recap of the last session, which covered
the #strong[Nawafil (نوافل)] \[supererogatory acts\] and #strong[Wajibat
(واجبات)] \[obligatory elements\] of Tawaf, including:

- Walking on foot (when capable) is a #strong[Wajib]\; it is waived in
  cases of illness or incapacity.
- Tawaf begins from #strong[Hajr al-Aswad (الحجر الأسود)] \[the Black
  Stone\], starting from its right side.
- Beginning from the right of Hajr al-Aswad is #strong[Wajib] in the
  Hanafi school and #strong[Sunnah] in the Shafi'i school. The dalil
  (evidence) for both is the same --- that the Prophet ﷺ always began
  Tawaf from the right of Hajr al-Aswad --- but the schools differ on
  the classification based on usul (principles of jurisprudence).

#horizontalrule

== 1. Ramal (رَمَل) \[Brisk Walking in Tawaf\]
<ramal-brisk-walking-in-tawaf>
#strong[Definition:] Ramal is a specific brisk, slightly hurried manner
of walking performed during the first three rounds of Tawaf.

#strong[When is it performed?]

- Ramal is performed in the #strong[Tawaf after which a Sa'i is to be
  performed].
- Normally, the first Tawaf performed upon arriving in Mecca ---
  #strong[Tawaf al-Qudum (طواف القدوم)] \[the Arrival Tawaf\] --- is
  followed by Sa'i, so Ramal is done in that Tawaf.
- If a person intends to perform #strong[Sa'i after Tawaf al-Ziyarah
  (طواف الزيارة)] \[the Obligatory Tawaf of Hajj\], they should perform
  Ramal in it as well. Otherwise, it is not done.

#strong[Status:] Ramal is a #strong[Sunnah], not a Wajib.

#horizontalrule

== 2. Sunan (سُنَن) \[Sunnahs\] of Tawaf
<sunan-sunnahs-of-tawaf>
=== a. Avoiding Unnecessary Talk
<a-avoiding-unnecessary-talk>
- During Tawaf, a person should be engaged in #strong[dhikr (ذِكر)]
  \[remembrance of Allah\], #strong[du'a (دُعاء)] \[supplication\], and
  #strong[istighfar (اِستغفار)] \[seeking forgiveness\].
- Tawaf is likened to #strong[Salah] in terms of maintaining reverence
  --- unnecessary speech should be minimized.
- Normal speech is #strong[Makruh (مكروه)] \[disliked\] if it distracts
  from dhikr; it is not outright forbidden.

=== b. Quran Recitation vs.~Dhikr --- Which is Better?
<b-quran-recitation-vs-dhikr-which-is-better>
A student raised a question: is it better to recite Quran or do
tasbeeh/dhikr during Tawaf?

#strong[Teacher's response:]

- Reciting the Quran is #strong[permissible] and generally considered
  the best act of worship.
- However, based on a position attributed to #strong[Imam Muhammad (رحمه
  الله)], he used the word #strong["لا حرج" (no objection)] regarding
  Quran recitation during Tawaf --- a phrase he typically reserves for
  acts that are merely permissible, not those that are optimal.
- Based on this, #strong[the preferred opinion] is that #strong[dhikr
  and du'a are more appropriate (Aula)] during Tawaf, while Quran
  recitation is permissible but not the preferred choice in this
  context.

=== c.~Performing Tawaf While Wearing Sandals
<c-performing-tawaf-while-wearing-sandals>
- It is #strong[permissible] to perform Tawaf while wearing sandals,
  provided they are #strong[pure (tahir)], meaning free from any
  impurity (najasat).
- #strong[Evidence:] It is reported that the Prophet ﷺ performed Tawaf
  while wearing sandals.
- #strong[Context:] After completing the acts of Nahar day (sacrifice,
  Halq/shaving), most restrictions of Ihram are lifted. The remaining
  restriction is sexual relations, which is removed by Tawaf al-Ziyarah.
  Since Tawaf is likened to Salah, and it is permissible to pray in pure
  sandals, Tawaf in sandals is also permissible --- in fact, Tawaf
  carries more ease (yusur) than Salah.

#horizontalrule

== 3. Place of Tawaf --- Boundaries
<place-of-tawaf-boundaries>
=== a. Within Masjid al-Haram
<a-within-masjid-al-haram>
- Tawaf must be performed #strong[within the boundaries of Masjid
  al-Haram]. It does not matter which part of the Masjid one is in ---
  near Zamzam, near the walls, etc. --- as long as one is within the
  Masjid boundaries.
- If someone performs Tawaf #strong[outside the Masjid], they are
  effectively making Tawaf of the Masjid, not of the Ka'bah. This is not
  valid.
- The walls of the Masjid act as a #strong[barrier], and Tawaf outside
  it is insufficient.

=== b. The Hatim (الحطيم) \[the Semicircular Wall\]
<b-the-hatim-the-semicircular-wall>
A crucial point: #strong[the Hatim is part of the Ka'bah (Baytullah)].

#strong[Historical background:]

#quote(block: true)[
The Ka'bah was originally constructed by Ibrahim (عليه السلام) to
include the Hatim area. However, due to limited resources when the
Quraysh later rebuilt it, the Hatim portion was left outside the main
structure. The Prophet ﷺ expressed a wish to restore it but refrained
--- as narrated to Sayyidah Aisha (رضي الله عنها) --- out of concern
that people who had recently embraced Islam might not accept such a
significant change and could revert to disbelief. Later, it was changed
by certain rulers, then changed back. Imam Ali (رحمه الله) subsequently
issued a fatwa that #strong[no one may change the structure of the
Ka'bah] after this --- it should remain as it is.
]

#strong[Implication for Tawaf:]

- Since the Hatim is part of Baytullah, a person making Tawaf
  #strong[must go around the outside of the Hatim] --- i.e., their path
  must include the Hatim within the circle of Tawaf.
- If someone walks #strong[through] the Hatim (inside the U-shape), they
  have not made Tawaf of that side of the Ka'bah and their Tawaf is
  #strong[invalid].

#strong[Evidence that the Hatim is part of Baytullah:]

- A hadith (as cited in class) states that the Hatim is part of
  Baytullah.
- This is supported by a well-known fatwa that a person who makes a
  #strong[nadhr (نذر)] \[vow\] to pray inside the Ka'bah can fulfill it
  by praying inside the Hatim area, since it is considered part of
  Baytullah.
- Similarly, the Prophet ﷺ instructed Sayyidah Aisha (رضي الله عنها) and
  others to pray two rak'ahs inside the Hatim to fulfill this type of
  nadhr.

=== c.~Why the Hatim Counts for Tawaf but NOT for Qibla Direction
<c-why-the-hatim-counts-for-tawaf-but-not-for-qibla-direction>
A conceptual question was addressed in class:

#strong[Q:] If the Hatim is part of Baytullah, why can a person facing
only the Hatim (not the main structure) not use it as their Qibla for
Salah?

#strong[A:] The command to face the #strong[Qibla (قبلة)] comes from the
Quran:

#quote(block: true)[
وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ

#emph["And wherever you are, turn your faces toward it \[the Sacred
Mosque\]."]

#strong[Ref:] Surah al-Baqarah: 144 #emph[\(as cited in class --- verify
ayah number)].
]

This is a #strong[Qat'i (قطعي)] \[categorical, definitive\] textual
command. The proof that the Hatim is part of Baytullah comes from a
#strong[Zanni (ظني)] \[probabilistic, speculative\] hadith.

In usul al-fiqh, a #strong[Zanni dalil cannot override a Qat'i command].
Therefore, when it comes to the direction of Salah, one must face the
main structure of the Ka'bah --- a Qat'i requirement --- and cannot rely
on the Hatim being part of it based on a Zanni proof.

However, for #strong[Tawaf], the Quran says:

#quote(block: true)[
وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ

#emph["And let them perform Tawaf around the Ancient House."]

#strong[Ref:] Surah al-Hajj: 29 #emph[\(as cited in class)].
]

Making Tawaf outside the Hatim #strong[does not contradict this ayah]
--- one is still going around the whole Baytullah, including the Hatim
as proven by hadith. So in Tawaf, we can act upon #strong[both] the
Quranic ayah and the hadith simultaneously. There is no contradiction.

#horizontalrule

== 4. Timing of Tawaf al-Ziyarah
<timing-of-tawaf-al-ziyarah>
=== Beginning Time
<beginning-time>
- #strong[Hanafi view (preferred):] Tawaf al-Ziyarah begins with the
  #strong[Fajr of the 10th of Dhul-Hijjah (يوم النحر)] \[the Day of
  Sacrifice\]. It is not valid before this.
- #strong[Imam al-Shafi'i's view:] It begins from the #strong[middle of
  the night] preceding the 10th of Dhul-Hijjah.

#strong[Hanafi response to Shafi'i:] The night between the 9th and 10th
is the time for #strong[Muzdalifah (مزدلفة)] --- specifically for Wuquf
al-Muzdalifah and Rami. Two different actions cannot share the same
window as their respective times. Therefore, Tawaf cannot begin until
Fajr of the 10th.

=== Ending Time
<ending-time>
- #strong[Preferred Hanafi view:] Tawaf al-Ziyarah must be completed
  #strong[before sunset of the 12th of Dhul-Hijjah], i.e., within the
  #strong[Ayyam al-Nahr (أيام النحر)] \[Days of Sacrifice: 10th, 11th,
  and 12th\].
- If delayed past this without a valid Shari'i excuse, the #strong[Wajib
  is missed], and a #strong[dam (دم)] \[penalty --- slaughter of an
  animal\] becomes obligatory.
- #strong[Imam al-Shafi'i and the Sahibayn (صاحبين)] \[Imam Abu Yusuf
  and Imam Muhammad --- the two companions of Imam Abu Hanifa\]: There
  is #strong[no ending time] for Tawaf al-Ziyarah. Whenever performed,
  it is valid without penalty.

#strong[Hanafi dalil (evidence) against the Sahibayn's position:]

The Sahibayn cite ahadith from #strong[Hajjat al-Wada'] in which the
Prophet ﷺ responded to people who performed Hajj actions out of order by
saying: #emph["No harm, no harm."] They argue this implies no time
limitation.

Imam Abu Hanifa's response: That leniency was a #strong[Takhfif (تخفيف)]
\[concession\] granted in the early days when the Ummah was just
learning the rites of Hajj. Once Shari'ah was established and awareness
spread, those fixed timings became binding --- just as the times of
Salah are fixed and cannot be missed without penalty.

#strong[Analogy with Salah:] Just as missing a Salah after its time
passes does not eliminate the obligation (it remains due as qada) but
incurs sin for the missed Wajib, similarly, performing Tawaf al-Ziyarah
after the 12th still fulfills the Fard --- but the Wajib of timely
performance is missed, and dam is due.

=== Best Day
<best-day>
The #strong[best day to perform Tawaf al-Ziyarah is the 10th of
Dhul-Hijjah], as the Prophet ﷺ performed it on that day. Performing it
early: 1. Fulfills the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ. 2. Removes the remaining
restriction of #strong[physical relations with one's spouse] --- the
last restriction of Ihram --- as early as possible.

#horizontalrule

== 5. How Much of Tawaf al-Ziyarah is Fard vs.~Wajib?
<how-much-of-tawaf-al-ziyarah-is-fard-vs-wajib>
#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (38.46%, 61.54%),
    align: (auto,auto,),
    table.header([Category], [Amount Required],),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Fard (فرض)] \[obligatory minimum\]], [#strong[Majority] of
    the Tawaf = at least 3 complete rounds + more than half of the 4th
    round],
    [#strong[Wajib (واجب)] \[obligatory completion\]], [All #strong[7
    rounds] of Tawaf al-Ziyarah],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

#strong[Key implication:] If a person completes the majority of Tawaf
(Fard portion) but not all 7 rounds: - The Fard is achieved. - The
missing rounds are a Wajib violation. - A #strong[dam] is required, but
the Hajj is not invalidated.

#strong[Imam al-Shafi'i's view:] All 7 rounds are Fard. His dalil: the
Prophet ﷺ performed 7 rounds. Additionally, the Quranic ayah
#emph["perform Tawaf around the Ancient House"] --- when the order is
given without specification of number, acting upon it even once is
sufficient. The 7 rounds are proven by the Prophet's practice.

#strong[Hanafi response:] The practice of the Prophet ﷺ establishes the
7 rounds through #strong[Khabar al-Wahid (خبر الواحد)] \[a hadith with a
single chain\], which can elevate an act to #strong[Wajib] but not to
#strong[Fard]. Fard requires #strong[Qat'i] proof. The Fard level
(majority) is based on #strong[Ijma' (إجماع)] \[scholarly consensus\].

#strong[Principle cited by the teacher:]

#quote(block: true)[
In Hajj, the majority of an act is treated like the complete act ---
especially in acts that lift the restrictions of Ihram.
]

#strong[Examples of this principle:] - In #strong[Dhabh (ذبح)]
\[slaughter\], slaughtering the majority of the required veins removes
Ihram restrictions. - In #strong[Rami al-Jamarat (رمي الجمرات)]
\[throwing pebbles\], throwing the majority removes most restrictions.

#horizontalrule

== 6. Case Scenarios --- Violations During or After Tawaf
<case-scenarios-violations-during-or-after-tawaf>
=== Case 1: Physical Relations After Majority of Tawaf but Before Completion
<case-1-physical-relations-after-majority-of-tawaf-but-before-completion>
- If a person completed the #strong[majority (Fard portion)] of Tawaf
  al-Ziyarah and then violated the restriction of physical relations:
  - #strong[Fard is complete] → Hajj is not nullified.
  - Violation occurred after Fard → penalty is a #strong[dam] (slaughter
    of a goat/sheep --- a medium-sized animal).

=== Case 2: Physical Relations Before Majority of Tawaf
<case-2-physical-relations-before-majority-of-tawaf>
- If a person violated physical relations after only 1--3 rounds (before
  the majority was completed):
  - Violation occurred before the Fard was achieved.
  - Penalty is a #strong[large animal (badanah)] --- a camel, cow, or
    buffalo.
  - According to Imam al-Shafi'i, the penalty is badanah in all cases
    since all 7 rounds are Fard.

#horizontalrule

== 7. Rulings for Missing or Defective Tawaf al-Ziyarah
<rulings-for-missing-or-defective-tawaf-al-ziyarah>
=== A. Complete Omission (Returning Home Without Performing It)
<a-complete-omission-returning-home-without-performing-it>
Since Tawaf al-Ziyarah is the #strong[second and final Fard of Hajj]
(after Wuquf al-Arafah), it #strong[cannot be replaced by anything].

- Hajj remains #strong[incomplete].
- The person must #strong[return to Mecca] to perform it --- no matter
  how much time passes.
- Until it is performed, #strong[physical relations with one's spouse
  remain Haram (حرام)] for life.
- Every time the person has relations with their spouse without
  completing Tawaf al-Ziyarah, a new #strong[dam] becomes obligatory.
- If a person becomes unable to return in their lifetime, they must
  #strong[arrange for it to be performed on their behalf (Hajj Badal بدل
  الحج)].

=== B. Partial Omission --- Performed After the 12th of Dhul-Hijjah
<b-partial-omission-performed-after-the-12th-of-dhul-hijjah>
- If performed after the time (after sunset on the 12th) #strong[without
  a valid Shari'i excuse] (illness, menstruation, nifas, emergency):
  - Tawaf is #strong[valid] --- Fard is fulfilled.
  - A #strong[dam] is due for missing the Wajib of timely performance.
- If delayed due to a #strong[valid Shari'i excuse] (severe illness,
  hayd/nifas for women, medical emergency):
  - Dam is #strong[waived].

#quote(block: true)[
#strong[Note:] Tawaf al-Ziyarah, unlike most Hajj acts, has #strong[no
expiry] in terms of the Fard itself. It can be performed #strong[any
time of year] --- even years later. The person remains under Ihram
restrictions until it is performed.
]

=== C. Tawaf Performed in a State of Janabah (جنابة) \[Major Ritual Impurity\]
<c-tawaf-performed-in-a-state-of-janabah-major-ritual-impurity>
- If the #strong[entire Tawaf] was performed in a state of Janabah:
  - The #strong[more emphasized] ruling (azimah) is to #strong[return to
    Mecca and repeat] the Tawaf.
  - The person's Ihram restrictions are still lifted (since the Tawaf
    was technically performed), and they would enter Mecca without a new
    Ihram. However, if they cross the Miqat without Ihram for a new
    purpose, another dam becomes due.
  - A #strong[badanah (بدنة)] \[large animal: camel, cow, or buffalo\]
    must be slaughtered in the Haram as well, because Janabah is a major
    defect.

=== D. Tawaf Performed Without Wudu (Minor Ritual Impurity Only)
<d-tawaf-performed-without-wudu-minor-ritual-impurity-only>
- If all 7 rounds were completed but without wudu:
  - Returning and repeating is the #strong[better] option, but not
    strictly required.
  - The #strong[defect is lesser] (minor impurity vs.~Janabah), so a
    #strong[dam] in the form of #strong[a goat/sheep (shatt)]
    slaughtered within the boundaries of the Haram is sufficient if
    returning is not possible.
  - The animal must be slaughtered #strong[in the Haram] ---
    slaughtering at home is not sufficient. The person sends money to a
    trustworthy person in Mecca to slaughter on their behalf.
  - In this case, #strong[sending the animal (rather than returning)] is
    more appropriate since the defect is minor.

=== E. Missing Rounds --- Not Reaching the Majority
<e-missing-rounds-not-reaching-the-majority>
- If a person performed only #strong[1, 2, or 3 rounds] of Tawaf
  al-Ziyarah --- i.e., did not complete the majority --- the Tawaf is
  #strong[not counted at all].
- It is treated as if Tawaf was not performed. The person must return
  and complete the full Tawaf.

=== F. Walking Through the Hatim
<f-walking-through-the-hatim>
- If a person walked #strong[inside the Hatim] (passing through the
  U-shaped area) instead of going around it during Tawaf:
  - Their Tawaf is incomplete --- they missed making Tawaf of one side
    of the Ka'bah.
  - They must #strong[repeat the Tawaf] (the full round, going around
    the outside of the Hatim).
  - If already back home: this is treated as having missed
    #strong[one-fourth] of the Tawaf → a #strong[dam] is required.

